e served content in headless Chrome and dump the DOM (`/tmp/wc-dump.html`) to inspect the actual display problem. Chrome available at `/usr/bin/google-chrome-stable`.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- `weather-card.js` exports `renderWeatherCard`, `renderWeatherGrid`, `renderWeatherGridToElement`, `injectStyles`, plus `unitOf`, `resolveCondition`, `codeToCondition`.\n- Rich data→card logic: `ICONS`, `GRADIENTS`, `LIGHT`, `WMO_CODE_MAP`, `WMO_ZH`, `KEYWORD_RULES`, `themeFor`, `statRows`, `hourlyRow`. Handles condition codes, hourly forecast, daily trend.\n- Sample data: Tokyo (partly-cloudy, hourly forecast), Reykjavík (thunderstorm, no hourly), Dubai (clear, hourly).\n- The `start-server.js` was the source of a prior EADDRINUSE error; the running instance is the persistent server, not this instance.\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- **External:** Port 10000 bound by prior instance (process owned by Mainthread). Do not kill/restart.\n- **Tool state:** No background tasks running (checked via `manage_task list`). Created temp harness `/tmp/wc-harness.html` and launch args `/tmp/wc-launch.args` for DOM inspection.\n- **Hypothesis:** The display issue is likely in the rendered output — need to inspect `/tmp/wc-dump.html` to confirm exact bug (empty grid, layout, or text rendering). Not yet confirmed.\n\n## 5. Next Steps (priority order)\n1. **Inspect `/tmp/wc-dump.html`** to see the actual rendered DOM and identify the display bug.\n2. If DOM is empty/malformed: debug `renderWeatherGridToElement`/`injectStyles` in `weather-card.js`.\n3. If DOM renders but looks wrong: fix CSS (`CARD_CSS`) — e.g., `.wc-grid`, `.wc` card styles.\n4. Overwrite the served `src/weather-card.js` and redeploy via the existing port-10000 server (restart it if needed).\n5. Re-verify all three endpoints return correct content types.\n\n## 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Do NOT start a second server on port 10000 (would EADDRINUSE).\n- Do NOT kill the existing healthy server instance.\n- Frontend is dependency-free ESM; edits must be valid JS modules.\n- User wants the display issue fixed and the deployment functional on 10000.\n\n</summary>\n\n# Conversation Logs\nStart with the compact transcript; if a step has `truncated_fields`, read only that specific line in `transcript_full.jsonl`:\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl`\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl`"}
